1
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:04,022
Water.

2
00:00:04,816 --> 00:00:06,316
Earth.

3
00:00:07,026 --> 00:00:08,360
Fire.

4
00:00:09,028 --> 00:00:10,279
Air.

5
00:00:11,155 --> 00:00:14,992
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,285 --> 00:00:19,162
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,706 --> 00:00:22,624
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:22,709 --> 00:00:23,709
could stop them.

9
00:00:23,793 --> 00:00:25,294
But when the world needed him most,

10
00:00:25,378 --> 00:00:26,878
he vanished.

11
00:00:27,422 --> 00:00:29,339
100 years passed, and my brother and I

12
00:00:29,424 --> 00:00:32,592
discovered the new Avatar,
an airbender named Aang.

13
00:00:32,885 --> 00:00:34,761
And although his airbending
skills are great,

14
00:00:34,846 --> 00:00:37,723
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

15
00:00:37,807 --> 00:00:39,016
Unh!

16
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:42,060
But I believe Aang can save the world.

17
00:01:01,956 --> 00:01:08,587
Unh!

18
00:01:18,306 --> 00:01:19,306
Where's Momo?

19
00:01:23,895 --> 00:01:24,978
Hang on, Momo!

20
00:01:39,285 --> 00:01:40,827
All right, you too.

21
00:01:41,704 --> 00:01:43,163
This is going to take forever.

22
00:01:46,584 --> 00:01:47,709
That works.

23
00:01:52,590 --> 00:01:53,590
These are Fire Nation traps.

24
00:01:54,092 --> 00:01:55,634
You can tell from the metalwork.

25
00:01:55,718 --> 00:01:57,594
We'd better pack up camp
and get moving.

26
00:01:59,597 --> 00:02:01,681
No flying this time.

27
00:02:01,766 --> 00:02:03,558
What? Why wouldn't we fly?

28
00:02:03,643 --> 00:02:04,768
Think about it.

29
00:02:04,852 --> 00:02:07,229
Somehow Prince Zuko
and the Fire Nation keep finding us.

30
00:02:07,563 --> 00:02:09,981
It's because they spot Appa,
he's just too noticeable.

31
00:02:10,066 --> 00:02:12,442
What? Appa's not too noticeable.

32
00:02:12,568 --> 00:02:15,278
He's a gigantic fluffy monster
with an arrow on his head!

33
00:02:15,405 --> 00:02:16,530
It's kind of hard to miss him.

34
00:02:18,324 --> 00:02:20,450
Sokka's just jealous
because he doesn't have an arrow.

35
00:02:20,785 --> 00:02:21,952
I know you all want to fly,

36
00:02:22,036 --> 00:02:23,120
but my instincts tell me

37
00:02:23,204 --> 00:02:24,871
we should play it safe
this time and walk.

38
00:02:25,164 --> 00:02:26,623
Who made you the boss?

39
00:02:26,707 --> 00:02:28,291
I'm not the boss, I'm the leader.

40
00:02:28,626 --> 00:02:30,627
You're the leader?

41
00:02:30,711 --> 00:02:32,671
But your voice still cracks.

42
00:02:32,755 --> 00:02:34,714
I'm the oldest, and I'm a warrior!

43
00:02:34,799 --> 00:02:36,591
So I'm the leader.

44
00:02:36,676 --> 00:02:38,510
If anyone's the leader, it's Aang.

45
00:02:38,719 --> 00:02:40,470
I mean, he is the Avatar.

46
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:42,639
Are you kidding?
He's just a goofy kid.

47
00:02:43,808 --> 00:02:44,933
He's right.

48
00:02:45,435 --> 00:02:47,853
Why do boys always think
someone has to be the leader?

49
00:02:48,521 --> 00:02:50,856
I bet you wouldn't be so bossy
if you kissed a girl.

50
00:02:51,149 --> 00:02:52,357
I've kissed a girl!

51
00:02:52,442 --> 00:02:53,567
You just haven't met her.

52
00:02:53,651 --> 00:02:55,777
Who? Gran-Gran?

53
00:02:55,862 --> 00:02:57,320
I've met Gran-Gran.

54
00:02:57,405 --> 00:02:58,822
No, besides Gran-Gran.

55
00:02:58,906 --> 00:03:00,949
Look, my instincts tell me

56
00:03:01,033 --> 00:03:02,784
we have a better chance
of slipping through on foot,

57
00:03:02,869 --> 00:03:04,619
and a leader has to
trust his instincts.

58
00:03:04,704 --> 00:03:08,123
Ok, we'll try it your way,
O wise leader.

59
00:03:08,332 --> 00:03:10,041
Who knows? Walking might be fun.

60
00:03:11,210 --> 00:03:12,544
Walking stinks!

61
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:15,130
How did people go anywhere
without a flying bison?

62
00:03:15,214 --> 00:03:16,673
I don't know, Aang.

63
00:03:16,757 --> 00:03:18,383
Why don't you ask Sokka's instincts?

64
00:03:18,593 --> 00:03:20,385
They seem to know everything.

65
00:03:20,595 --> 00:03:21,928
Ha ha, very funny.

66
00:03:22,138 --> 00:03:24,055
I'm tired of carrying this pack.

67
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:26,558
You know who you should
ask to carry it for a while?

68
00:03:26,767 --> 00:03:28,018
Sokka's instincts!

69
00:03:28,227 --> 00:03:29,769
That's a great idea.

70
00:03:30,188 --> 00:03:31,980
Hey, Sokka's instincts,
would you mind--

71
00:03:32,064 --> 00:03:33,773
Ok, ok, I get it!

72
00:03:33,858 --> 00:03:35,525
Look, guys, I'm tired, too.

73
00:03:35,610 --> 00:03:38,612
But the important thing is that
we're safe from the Fire Nation.

74
00:03:43,826 --> 00:03:44,826
Run!

75
00:03:49,332 --> 00:03:50,332
We're cut off!

76
00:03:50,416 --> 00:03:51,583
Sokka, your shirt!

77
00:03:51,667 --> 00:03:52,667
Aah!

78
00:04:00,718 --> 00:04:03,261
If you let us pass,
we promise not to hurt you.

79
00:04:03,721 --> 00:04:04,971
What are you doing?

80
00:04:05,056 --> 00:04:06,389
Bluffing.

81
00:04:06,766 --> 00:04:08,850
You, promise not to hurt us?

82
00:04:08,935 --> 00:04:09,935
Unh.

83
00:04:12,188 --> 00:04:14,564
Nice work, Sokka. How did you do that?

84
00:04:14,649 --> 00:04:16,441
Instinct?

85
00:04:16,859 --> 00:04:17,859
Look!

86
00:04:28,204 --> 00:04:29,204
Unh!

87
00:04:29,830 --> 00:04:30,914
Down you go.

88
00:04:36,963 --> 00:04:38,463
They're in the trees!

89
00:04:38,548 --> 00:04:39,548
Ha ha ha!

90
00:04:54,772 --> 00:04:57,232
Hah!

91
00:04:57,316 --> 00:04:58,316
Unh!

92
00:04:58,401 --> 00:04:59,526
Hey, he was mine.

93
00:04:59,944 --> 00:05:01,278
Gotta be quicker next time.

94
00:05:09,370 --> 00:05:10,704
Unh!

95
00:05:22,300 --> 00:05:23,300
Man!

96
00:05:32,852 --> 00:05:34,019
Hey.

97
00:05:34,103 --> 00:05:35,103
Hi.

98
00:05:39,150 --> 00:05:41,318
You just took out a whole army
almost single-handed.

99
00:05:41,402 --> 00:05:42,736
Army?!

100
00:05:42,820 --> 00:05:45,030
There were only, like, 20 guys.

101
00:05:45,698 --> 00:05:46,865
My name is Jet,

102
00:05:46,949 --> 00:05:48,199
and these are my freedom fighters.

103
00:05:48,618 --> 00:05:51,870
Sneers, Longshot, Smellerbee,

104
00:05:52,288 --> 00:05:53,997
The Duke, and Pipsqueak.

105
00:05:54,624 --> 00:05:56,708
Pipsqueak, that's a funny name.

106
00:05:58,961 --> 00:06:01,212
You think my name is funny?

107
00:06:01,547 --> 00:06:02,964
It's hilarious!

108
00:06:07,678 --> 00:06:08,678
Unh!

109
00:06:20,524 --> 00:06:23,276
Um, thanks for saving us, Jet.

110
00:06:23,611 --> 00:06:24,819
We're lucky you were there.

111
00:06:24,904 --> 00:06:26,529
I should be thanking you.

112
00:06:26,822 --> 00:06:29,032
We were waiting to ambush
those soldiers all morning.

113
00:06:29,367 --> 00:06:30,700
We just needed the right distraction.

114
00:06:30,785 --> 00:06:32,369
And then you guys stumbled in.

115
00:06:32,453 --> 00:06:34,496
We were relying on instincts.

116
00:06:34,789 --> 00:06:36,331
You'll get yourself
killed doing that.

117
00:06:41,462 --> 00:06:44,547
Hey, Jet, these barrels are filled
with blasting jelly.

118
00:06:44,632 --> 00:06:46,091
That's a great score.

119
00:06:46,425 --> 00:06:48,968
And these boxes are filled
with jellied candy.

120
00:06:49,303 --> 00:06:50,720
Also good.

121
00:06:50,805 --> 00:06:52,055
Let's not get those mixed up.

122
00:06:52,390 --> 00:06:53,848
We'll take the stuff
back to the hideout.

123
00:06:54,350 --> 00:06:55,642
You guys have a hideout?

124
00:06:56,018 --> 00:06:57,018
You want to see it?

125
00:06:57,103 --> 00:06:58,103
Yes, we want to see it!

126
00:07:02,191 --> 00:07:03,274
We're here.

127
00:07:03,484 --> 00:07:04,984
Where? There's nothing here.

128
00:07:05,236 --> 00:07:06,236
Hold this.

129
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:07,529
Why? What's this do?

130
00:07:07,780 --> 00:07:09,489
Aah!

131
00:07:09,573 --> 00:07:10,615
Aang?

132
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:11,866
I'll get up on my own.

133
00:07:15,996 --> 00:07:17,330
Grab hold of me, Katara.

134
00:07:31,470 --> 00:07:32,846
Nice place you got!

135
00:07:39,270 --> 00:07:40,645
It's beautiful up here.

136
00:07:40,730 --> 00:07:42,856
It's beautiful, and more importantly,

137
00:07:42,940 --> 00:07:44,482
the Fire Nation can't find us.

138
00:07:44,567 --> 00:07:46,234
They would love to find you,

139
00:07:46,318 --> 00:07:47,610
wouldn't they, Jet?

140
00:07:47,695 --> 00:07:49,404
It's not going to happen, Smellerbee.

141
00:07:49,697 --> 00:07:51,531
Why does the Fire Nation
want to find you?

142
00:07:51,615 --> 00:07:52,991
I guess you could say

143
00:07:53,075 --> 00:07:54,576
I've been causing them
a little trouble.

144
00:07:54,660 --> 00:07:56,703
See, they took over a nearby
Earth Kingdom town

145
00:07:56,787 --> 00:07:57,787
a few years back.

146
00:07:58,122 --> 00:07:59,456
We've been ambushing their troops,

147
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:01,124
cutting off their supply lines,

148
00:08:01,208 --> 00:08:03,585
and doing anything we can
to mess with them.

149
00:08:03,961 --> 00:08:05,420
One day, we'll drive the Fire Nation

150
00:08:05,504 --> 00:08:06,504
out of here for good,

151
00:08:06,589 --> 00:08:07,589
And free that town.

152
00:08:07,673 --> 00:08:09,466
That's so brave.

153
00:08:09,550 --> 00:08:12,302
Yeah, nothing's braver
than a guy in a tree house.

154
00:08:12,595 --> 00:08:14,262
Don't pay any attention to my brother.

155
00:08:14,597 --> 00:08:16,765
No problem. He probably
had a rough day.

156
00:08:16,849 --> 00:08:18,391
So, you all live here?

157
00:08:18,476 --> 00:08:19,476
That's right.

158
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:20,935
Longshot over there,

159
00:08:21,228 --> 00:08:23,438
His town got burned down
by the Fire Nation.

160
00:08:23,647 --> 00:08:25,565
And we found The Duke
trying to steal our food.

161
00:08:26,108 --> 00:08:27,942
I don't think he ever
really had a home.

162
00:08:28,277 --> 00:08:29,527
What about you?

163
00:08:31,405 --> 00:08:32,989
The Fire Nation killed my parents.

164
00:08:33,741 --> 00:08:35,575
I was only eight years old.

165
00:08:35,951 --> 00:08:37,660
That day changed me forever.

166
00:08:37,745 --> 00:08:40,663
Sokka and I lost our mother
to the Fire Nation.

167
00:08:40,873 --> 00:08:42,749
I'm so sorry, Katara.

168
00:08:53,260 --> 00:08:55,637
Today, we struck another blow

169
00:08:55,721 --> 00:08:57,055
against the Fire Nation swine.

170
00:09:00,893 --> 00:09:03,812
I got a special joy
from the look on one soldier's face,

171
00:09:03,896 --> 00:09:05,355
when The Duke dropped down
on his helmet

172
00:09:05,439 --> 00:09:07,899
and rode him like a wild hog-monkey!

173
00:09:13,030 --> 00:09:15,281
Now, the Fire Nation
thinks they don't have to worry

174
00:09:15,366 --> 00:09:17,742
about a couple of kids
hiding in the trees.

175
00:09:18,202 --> 00:09:19,702
Maybe they're right.

176
00:09:23,791 --> 00:09:27,252
Or maybe, they're dead wrong.

177
00:09:32,132 --> 00:09:33,925
Hey, Jet, nice speech.

178
00:09:34,009 --> 00:09:35,176
Thanks.

179
00:09:35,678 --> 00:09:36,678
By the way,

180
00:09:36,762 --> 00:09:38,137
I was really impressed
with you and Aang.

181
00:09:38,222 --> 00:09:40,181
That was some great bending
I saw out there today.

182
00:09:40,266 --> 00:09:43,059
Well, he's great. He's the Avatar.

183
00:09:43,561 --> 00:09:44,853
I could use some more training.

184
00:09:45,312 --> 00:09:48,106
Avatar, huh? Very nice.

185
00:09:48,482 --> 00:09:49,607
Thanks, Jet.

186
00:09:50,025 --> 00:09:51,025
So I might know a way

187
00:09:51,110 --> 00:09:52,527
that you and Aang
can help in our struggle.

188
00:09:52,611 --> 00:09:54,863
Unfortunately,
we have to leave tonight.

189
00:09:55,614 --> 00:09:56,948
Sokka, you're kidding me.

190
00:09:57,032 --> 00:09:59,576
I needed you on an important
mission tomorrow.

191
00:10:00,077 --> 00:10:01,077
What mission?

192
00:10:15,301 --> 00:10:16,593
What are you doing?

193
00:10:16,677 --> 00:10:18,595
Shh. It amplifies vibrations.

194
00:10:18,679 --> 00:10:19,846
Good trick.

195
00:10:20,472 --> 00:10:22,015
Nothing yet.

196
00:10:22,349 --> 00:10:23,391
Wait, yes!

197
00:10:23,475 --> 00:10:24,475
Someone's approaching.

198
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:25,643
How many?

199
00:10:25,728 --> 00:10:26,895
I think there's just one.

200
00:10:29,064 --> 00:10:30,857
Good work, Sokka. Ready your weapon.

201
00:10:35,821 --> 00:10:37,155
Wait! False alarm.

202
00:10:37,239 --> 00:10:38,448
He's just an old man.

203
00:10:43,871 --> 00:10:45,705
What are you doing
in our woods, you leech?

204
00:10:45,789 --> 00:10:48,583
Please, sir, I'm just a traveler.

205
00:10:51,754 --> 00:10:53,171
Unh!

206
00:10:58,677 --> 00:11:00,011
Do you like destroying towns?

207
00:11:00,095 --> 00:11:01,638
Do you like destroying families?

208
00:11:01,722 --> 00:11:03,222
Do you?!

209
00:11:03,307 --> 00:11:06,768
Please, let me go. Have mercy.

210
00:11:07,102 --> 00:11:08,853
Does the Fire Nation let people go?

211
00:11:08,938 --> 00:11:10,605
Does the Fire Nation have mercy?

212
00:11:12,858 --> 00:11:14,275
Jet, he's just an old man!

213
00:11:14,360 --> 00:11:15,985
He's Fire Nation! Search him!

214
00:11:16,070 --> 00:11:17,904
But he's not hurting anyone.

215
00:11:17,988 --> 00:11:20,365
Have you forgotten that
the Fire Nation killed your mother?

216
00:11:20,449 --> 00:11:22,116
Remember why you fight!

217
00:11:22,201 --> 00:11:23,743
We got his stuff, Jet.

218
00:11:23,827 --> 00:11:25,620
This doesn't feel right.

219
00:11:25,704 --> 00:11:28,039
It's what has to be done.
Now let's get out of here.

220
00:11:32,836 --> 00:11:33,836
Come on, Sokka!

221
00:11:38,968 --> 00:11:41,094
Sokka, look what The Duke gave me.

222
00:11:48,477 --> 00:11:50,019
Quit it!

223
00:11:50,688 --> 00:11:52,480
Hey, Sokka. Is Jet back?

224
00:11:52,856 --> 00:11:54,565
Yeah, he's back. But we're leaving.

225
00:11:54,650 --> 00:11:55,733
What?

226
00:11:55,818 --> 00:11:57,527
But I made him this hat.

227
00:11:58,320 --> 00:11:59,988
Your boyfriend Jet's a thug.

228
00:12:00,072 --> 00:12:01,072
What?!

229
00:12:01,156 --> 00:12:02,365
No, he's not.

230
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:04,075
He's messed up, Katara.

231
00:12:04,159 --> 00:12:05,284
He's not messed up.

232
00:12:05,369 --> 00:12:07,036
He's just got a different way of life.

233
00:12:07,121 --> 00:12:08,579
A really fun way of life.

234
00:12:08,872 --> 00:12:10,039
He beat and robbed

235
00:12:10,124 --> 00:12:11,290
a harmless old man.

236
00:12:12,084 --> 00:12:14,293
I want to hear
Jet's side of the story.

237
00:12:15,212 --> 00:12:16,754
Sokka, you told them what happened,

238
00:12:16,839 --> 00:12:19,298
but you didn't mention
that the guy was Fire Nation?

239
00:12:19,383 --> 00:12:21,926
No, he conveniently
left that part out.

240
00:12:22,386 --> 00:12:24,220
Fine, but even if he was Fire Nation,

241
00:12:24,304 --> 00:12:25,596
he was a harmless civilian.

242
00:12:26,015 --> 00:12:27,223
He was an assassin, Sokka.

243
00:12:30,144 --> 00:12:32,854
See? There's a compartment
for poison in the knife.

244
00:12:32,938 --> 00:12:34,439
He was sent to eliminate me.

245
00:12:34,523 --> 00:12:36,441
You helped save my life, Sokka.

246
00:12:36,775 --> 00:12:38,401
I knew there was an explanation.

247
00:12:38,777 --> 00:12:40,194
I didn't see any knife.

248
00:12:40,654 --> 00:12:42,071
That's because he was concealing it.

249
00:12:42,156 --> 00:12:43,656
See, Sokka?

250
00:12:43,741 --> 00:12:45,867
I'm sure you just
didn't notice the knife.

251
00:12:45,951 --> 00:12:47,660
There was no knife!

252
00:12:47,870 --> 00:12:49,037
I'm going back to the hut

253
00:12:49,121 --> 00:12:50,455
and packing my things.

254
00:12:51,373 --> 00:12:52,874
Tell me you guys aren't leaving yet.

255
00:12:52,958 --> 00:12:54,417
I really need your help.

256
00:12:54,501 --> 00:12:55,543
What can we do?

257
00:12:55,919 --> 00:12:58,004
The Fire Nation is planning
on burning down our forest.

258
00:12:58,422 --> 00:13:00,339
If you both use waterbending
to fill the reservoir,

259
00:13:00,424 --> 00:13:01,716
we could fight the fires.

260
00:13:02,092 --> 00:13:03,342
But if you leave now,

261
00:13:03,427 --> 00:13:05,053
they'll destroy the whole valley.

262
00:13:09,224 --> 00:13:10,516
We can't leave now

263
00:13:10,601 --> 00:13:12,894
with the Fire Nation
about to burn down a forest!

264
00:13:12,978 --> 00:13:14,395
I'm sorry, Katara.

265
00:13:14,730 --> 00:13:16,481
Jet's very smooth,
but we can't trust him.

266
00:13:16,899 --> 00:13:18,483
You know what I think?

267
00:13:18,567 --> 00:13:21,277
You're jealous that he's a better
warrior and a better leader.

268
00:13:21,612 --> 00:13:23,529
Katara, I'm not jealous of Jet.

269
00:13:23,614 --> 00:13:24,739
It's just that my instincts--

270
00:13:24,823 --> 00:13:26,407
Well, my instincts tell me

271
00:13:26,492 --> 00:13:28,576
we need to stay here a little longer
and help Jet.

272
00:13:29,078 --> 00:13:30,244
Come on, Aang.

273
00:13:30,662 --> 00:13:31,662
Sorry, Sokka.

274
00:13:41,965 --> 00:13:42,965
Let's go.

275
00:14:05,656 --> 00:14:06,781
Now listen.

276
00:14:06,865 --> 00:14:08,991
You're not to blow the dam
until I give the signal.

277
00:14:09,076 --> 00:14:10,785
If the reservoir isn't full,

278
00:14:10,869 --> 00:14:12,662
the Fire Nation troops could survive.

279
00:14:13,330 --> 00:14:15,123
But what about the people in the town?

280
00:14:15,207 --> 00:14:17,041
Won't they get wiped out, too?

281
00:14:17,251 --> 00:14:18,793
Look, Duke, that's the price

282
00:14:18,877 --> 00:14:20,878
of ridding this area
of the Fire Nation.

283
00:14:21,213 --> 00:14:22,755
Now don't blow the dam
until I give the signal.

284
00:14:22,840 --> 00:14:23,840
Got it?

285
00:14:28,595 --> 00:14:31,264
Where do you think
you're going, ponytail?

286
00:14:36,603 --> 00:14:37,687
Sokka.

287
00:14:37,771 --> 00:14:39,939
I'm glad you decided to join us.

288
00:14:40,941 --> 00:14:43,526
I heard your plan
to destroy the Earth Kingdom town.

289
00:14:43,610 --> 00:14:46,028
Our plan is to rid the valley
of the Fire Nation.

290
00:14:46,113 --> 00:14:47,822
There are people living there, Jet,

291
00:14:47,906 --> 00:14:49,657
mothers and fathers and children.

292
00:14:50,117 --> 00:14:52,743
We can't win without
making some sacrifices.

293
00:14:52,828 --> 00:14:55,121
You lied to Aang and Katara
about the forest fire.

294
00:14:55,372 --> 00:14:57,456
Because they don't understand
the demands of war.

295
00:14:57,541 --> 00:14:58,958
Not like you and I do.

296
00:14:59,168 --> 00:15:00,501
I do understand.

297
00:15:00,586 --> 00:15:02,086
I understand that
there's nothing you won't do

298
00:15:02,171 --> 00:15:03,337
to get what you want.

299
00:15:03,922 --> 00:15:06,132
I was hoping you'd have an open mind.

300
00:15:06,216 --> 00:15:08,092
But I can see you've made your choice.

301
00:15:10,053 --> 00:15:12,013
I can't let you warn Katara and Aang.

302
00:15:12,097 --> 00:15:13,347
Take him for a walk.

303
00:15:13,557 --> 00:15:14,682
A long walk.

304
00:15:14,892 --> 00:15:16,517
You can't do this!

305
00:15:16,602 --> 00:15:17,935
Cheer up, Sokka.

306
00:15:18,228 --> 00:15:19,687
We're going to win a great victory

307
00:15:19,771 --> 00:15:20,897
against the Fire Nation today.

308
00:15:24,151 --> 00:15:26,903
Jet, I'm sorry about how
Sokka's been acting.

309
00:15:26,987 --> 00:15:29,363
No worries. He already apologized.

310
00:15:29,573 --> 00:15:31,949
Really? Sokka apologized?

311
00:15:32,326 --> 00:15:33,910
Yeah, I was surprised, too.

312
00:15:34,578 --> 00:15:35,703
I got the sense that maybe you

313
00:15:35,787 --> 00:15:36,787
Talked to him or something.

314
00:15:36,872 --> 00:15:37,997
Yeah, I did.

315
00:15:38,081 --> 00:15:39,749
I guess something you said
got through to him.

316
00:15:40,125 --> 00:15:42,084
Anyhow, he went out
on a scouting mission

317
00:15:42,169 --> 00:15:43,794
with Pipsqueak and Smellerbee.

318
00:15:43,879 --> 00:15:44,962
I'm glad he cooled off.

319
00:15:45,297 --> 00:15:47,006
He's so stubborn sometimes.

320
00:15:49,051 --> 00:15:50,301
All right, we're here.

321
00:15:50,719 --> 00:15:52,595
Underground water's trying
to escape from these vents.

322
00:15:53,096 --> 00:15:54,680
I need you guys to help it along.

323
00:15:54,973 --> 00:15:57,767
I've never used bending
on water I can't see.

324
00:15:57,851 --> 00:15:59,227
I don't know...

325
00:15:59,436 --> 00:16:01,896
Katara, you can do this.

326
00:16:02,105 --> 00:16:03,397
What about me?

327
00:16:03,607 --> 00:16:05,566
I know the Avatar can do this.

328
00:16:27,089 --> 00:16:28,756
Yes! Good job.

329
00:16:29,007 --> 00:16:30,591
This river empties into the reservoir.

330
00:16:30,676 --> 00:16:32,385
A few more geysers
and it will be full.

331
00:16:33,053 --> 00:16:35,054
Look, there's another steam vent.

332
00:16:36,139 --> 00:16:37,890
Ok, you two keep it up,

333
00:16:37,975 --> 00:16:39,475
I'll go check on things
at the reservoir.

334
00:16:41,186 --> 00:16:42,979
When we're done,
we'll meet you over there.

335
00:16:43,063 --> 00:16:45,189
Actually, probably better
if you meet me

336
00:16:45,274 --> 00:16:46,565
back at the hideout when you're done.

337
00:16:57,077 --> 00:16:58,536
I bet that's enough.

338
00:16:58,620 --> 00:17:00,079
And I'm not just
saying that to be lazy.

339
00:17:00,455 --> 00:17:02,206
Let's catch up with Jet
at the reservoir.

340
00:17:02,582 --> 00:17:04,542
I thought we agreed
to meet Jet back at the hideout.

341
00:17:04,626 --> 00:17:06,168
Well, we finished early.

342
00:17:06,586 --> 00:17:07,920
I'm sure he'll be happy to see us.

343
00:17:11,133 --> 00:17:13,175
Come on, move along!

344
00:17:13,260 --> 00:17:14,802
How can you stand by and do nothing

345
00:17:14,886 --> 00:17:16,721
while Jet wipes out a whole town?

346
00:17:17,055 --> 00:17:19,348
Hey, listen, Sokka,
Jet's a great leader.

347
00:17:19,433 --> 00:17:23,102
We follow what he says,
and things always turn out ok.

348
00:17:27,733 --> 00:17:29,358
If that's how Jet leads,

349
00:17:29,776 --> 00:17:30,943
Then he's got a lot to learn!

350
00:17:31,028 --> 00:17:32,028
Hey!

351
00:17:34,031 --> 00:17:35,031
Unh!

352
00:17:36,325 --> 00:17:37,533
While you two are up there,

353
00:17:37,617 --> 00:17:39,702
you might want to practice
your knot work.

354
00:17:40,579 --> 00:17:42,163
Hey, Smellerbee.

355
00:17:42,247 --> 00:17:44,165
You going to eat your lychee nuts?

356
00:17:44,249 --> 00:17:45,374
Ooh.

357
00:17:52,549 --> 00:17:53,632
What are they doing?

358
00:17:53,717 --> 00:17:55,092
Hey, those are the red barrels

359
00:17:55,177 --> 00:17:56,344
he got from the Fire Nation.

360
00:17:56,595 --> 00:17:58,387
Why would they need blasting jelly?

361
00:17:58,972 --> 00:18:01,057
Because Jet's going to
blow up the dam.

362
00:18:01,475 --> 00:18:02,475
What?

363
00:18:02,559 --> 00:18:04,352
No, that would destroy the town.

364
00:18:04,436 --> 00:18:06,020
Jet wouldn't do that.

365
00:18:06,104 --> 00:18:07,646
I've got to stop him!

366
00:18:08,148 --> 00:18:09,440
Jet wouldn't do that.

367
00:18:09,941 --> 00:18:10,983
Unh!

368
00:18:12,611 --> 00:18:13,652
Yes, I would.

369
00:18:13,737 --> 00:18:14,987
Jet, why?

370
00:18:15,072 --> 00:18:17,615
Katara, you would, too,
if you just stop to think.

371
00:18:18,283 --> 00:18:20,910
Think about what the Fire Nation
did to your mother.

372
00:18:20,994 --> 00:18:23,537
We can't let them do that
to anyone else ever again.

373
00:18:23,830 --> 00:18:25,539
This isn't the answer.

374
00:18:25,624 --> 00:18:27,792
I want you to understand me, Katara.

375
00:18:28,210 --> 00:18:30,336
I thought your brother
would understand, but--

376
00:18:30,712 --> 00:18:32,254
Where's Sokka?

377
00:18:32,339 --> 00:18:33,339
Katara.

378
00:18:36,134 --> 00:18:37,426
Unh!

379
00:18:40,180 --> 00:18:41,305
I need to get to the dam.

380
00:18:43,266 --> 00:18:45,226
You're not going anywhere
without your glider.

381
00:18:45,310 --> 00:18:46,727
Unh! Uhh! Unh!

382
00:18:48,855 --> 00:18:50,272
I'm not going to fight you, Jet.

383
00:18:50,357 --> 00:18:52,233
You'll have to
if you want your glider back.

384
00:19:01,410 --> 00:19:02,410
Hah!

385
00:19:06,206 --> 00:19:07,206
Unh!

386
00:19:13,672 --> 00:19:14,755
Hah!

387
00:19:28,103 --> 00:19:29,103
Aah!

388
00:19:30,105 --> 00:19:31,188
Unh!

389
00:19:31,273 --> 00:19:32,273
Aah!

390
00:19:54,212 --> 00:19:55,212
Unh!

391
00:20:05,432 --> 00:20:06,432
Aah!

392
00:20:06,516 --> 00:20:07,516
Unh!

393
00:20:14,483 --> 00:20:15,524
Unh!

394
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:31,874
Why, Jet?

395
00:20:31,958 --> 00:20:34,210
I can't believe I trusted you.

396
00:20:34,753 --> 00:20:36,045
You lied to me!

397
00:20:36,129 --> 00:20:38,088
You're sick, and I trusted you!

398
00:20:45,013 --> 00:20:46,180
What are you doing?

399
00:20:46,264 --> 00:20:47,264
You're too late.

400
00:20:47,349 --> 00:20:48,349
No!

401
00:20:51,603 --> 00:20:52,770
Unh!

402
00:20:54,231 --> 00:20:55,564
Sokka's still out there.

403
00:20:55,774 --> 00:20:57,358
He's our only chance.

404
00:20:57,442 --> 00:20:59,109
Come on, Sokka.

405
00:20:59,444 --> 00:21:01,111
I'm sorry I ever doubted you.

406
00:21:01,196 --> 00:21:02,196
Please...

407
00:21:09,788 --> 00:21:10,871
No.

408
00:21:30,600 --> 00:21:32,184
Sokka didn't make it in time.

409
00:21:32,269 --> 00:21:33,602
All those people.

410
00:21:34,604 --> 00:21:36,146
Jet, you monster!

411
00:21:36,231 --> 00:21:37,856
This was a victory, Katara.

412
00:21:37,941 --> 00:21:39,108
Remember that.

413
00:21:39,192 --> 00:21:40,568
The Fire Nation is gone,

414
00:21:40,652 --> 00:21:41,735
and this valley will be safe.

415
00:21:42,070 --> 00:21:43,445
It will be safe,

416
00:21:43,530 --> 00:21:45,281
without you.

417
00:21:46,032 --> 00:21:47,032
Sokka!

418
00:21:47,242 --> 00:21:48,617
I warned the villagers of your plan,

419
00:21:48,702 --> 00:21:49,702
Just in time.

420
00:21:49,786 --> 00:21:52,121
-What?!
-At first, they didn't believe me.

421
00:21:52,205 --> 00:21:54,790
The Fire Nation soldiers
assumed I was a spy.

422
00:21:54,874 --> 00:21:56,166
But one man vouched for me,

423
00:21:56,251 --> 00:21:58,294
the old man you attacked.

424
00:21:58,378 --> 00:22:01,505
He urged them to trust me,
and we got everyone out in time.

425
00:22:06,845 --> 00:22:08,846
Mrs. Pretty!

426
00:22:09,598 --> 00:22:10,973
Sokka, you fool!

427
00:22:11,057 --> 00:22:12,141
We could have freed this valley!

428
00:22:12,225 --> 00:22:13,392
Who would be free?

429
00:22:13,768 --> 00:22:14,893
Everyone would be dead.

430
00:22:15,353 --> 00:22:16,353
You traitor!

431
00:22:16,438 --> 00:22:18,230
No, Jet. You became the traitor

432
00:22:18,315 --> 00:22:20,190
when you stopped
protecting innocent people.

433
00:22:20,609 --> 00:22:23,110
Katara, please, help me.

434
00:22:23,361 --> 00:22:24,862
Good-bye, Jet.

435
00:22:25,530 --> 00:22:26,822
Yip, yip.

436
00:22:31,578 --> 00:22:33,037
We thought
you were going to the dam.

437
00:22:33,371 --> 00:22:34,872
How come you went to the town instead?

438
00:22:34,956 --> 00:22:36,206
Let me guess.

439
00:22:36,291 --> 00:22:37,875
Your instincts told you.

440
00:22:37,959 --> 00:22:39,460
Hey, sometimes they're right.

441
00:22:39,544 --> 00:22:41,211
Um, Sokka?

442
00:22:41,296 --> 00:22:43,130
You know we're going
the wrong way, right?

443
00:22:43,673 --> 00:22:45,341
And sometimes they're wrong.
